From: UPF maintainers <upf@omecproject.org>
Subject: [PATCH] python: allow a caller-provided Scapy distribution

TRex's Python bootstrap forces its bundled Scapy 2.4.3 onto sys.path.  That
causes mixed Scapy modules when UPF's PTF environment supplies its locked
Scapy distribution.  Do not add the bundled Scapy; callers are responsible
for installing a compatible Scapy distribution.

---
 scripts/automation/trex_control_plane/interactive/trex/__init__.py | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/automation/trex_control_plane/interactive/trex/__init__.py b/scripts/automation/trex_control_plane/interactive/trex/__init__.py
index 8df5bea..4df3464 100644
--- a/scripts/automation/trex_control_plane/interactive/trex/__init__.py
+++ b/scripts/automation/trex_control_plane/interactive/trex/__init__.py
@@ -30,7 +30,6 @@ def __load ():
     ext_libs = [ {'name': 'texttable',    'dir': 'texttable-0.8.4'},
                  {'name': 'yaml',         'dir': 'pyyaml-3.11', 'py-dep': True},
-                 {'name': 'scapy',        'dir': 'scapy-2.4.3'},
                  {'name': 'zmq',          'dir': 'pyzmq-ctypes'},
                  {'name': 'simpy',        'dir': 'simpy-3.0.10'},
                  {'name': 'trex_openssl', 'dir': 'trex-openssl'},
